# Undefined Behavior Sanitizer suppressions for scripts/weekly_sanitizer.py
# (UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>). Same contract as tsan.supp: each entry is a
# KNOWN finding with an open issue (`# known:` line, `# reason:` lines, one pattern);
# the runner refuses anything else and the card shows it grey.

# known: code=mlx-null-linked-functions issue=463 date=2026-11-08 repro=MLXSafetyTests
# reason: mlx-swift 0.29.1 device.cpp:717 calls mtl_linked_funcs->release() when
# reason: get_linked_functions_() returned nullptr (a kernel with no linked functions).
# reason: The body is objc_msgSend(nil, release): a no-op at runtime, formally UB.
# reason: Not a missing Metal device. Gone in mlx-swift 0.33.0 (smart pointers).
# reason: UBSan checks that one call twice: at device.cpp:717, then inside the inlined
# reason: release() at metal-cpp Foundation/NSObject.hpp:112:49 (the 2026-11-14 run read
# reason: red for the second while a device.cpp file pattern silenced only the first).
# reason: Matched by FUNCTION, the reporting PC of both (frame #0): any null-pointer
# reason: check in get_kernel_, nothing else in device.cpp, nothing else in metal-cpp
# reason: (NSObject.hpp is every metal-cpp object's release; a file pattern on it would
# reason: hide any null release anywhere). A build whose symbolizer resolves the inlined
# reason: frame (frame #0 = NS::Referencing<…>::release) will print the second report
# reason: again: that reads red, never hidden.
null:mlx::core::metal::Device::get_kernel_
